✅ EXACT COMMANDS (copy/paste)
1) Cloud context + namespaces (proves you’re on DOKS)
cd "D:\Shoaib Project\nimbus-tasks"
kubectl config current-context
kubectl get ns

2) Pods + rollout status (proves all workloads are healthy)
kubectl -n nimbus get pods -o wide
kubectl -n nimbus rollout status deploy/nimbus-backend
kubectl -n nimbus rollout status deploy/nimbus-worker
kubectl -n nimbus rollout status deploy/nimbus-frontend

3) Dapr sidecar + image proof (proves Dapr enabled + correct images)
kubectl -n nimbus describe pod -l app=nimbus-backend | Select-String "dapr.io/app-id|Containers:|backend:|daprd:|Image:"
kubectl -n nimbus describe pod -l app=nimbus-worker  | Select-String "dapr.io/app-id|Containers:|worker:|daprd:|Image:"

4) Dapr components exist (pubsub + cron + secretstore)
kubectl -n nimbus get components

5) Ingress routes (proves /api → backend, / → frontend)
kubectl -n nimbus get ingress
kubectl -n nimbus describe ingress nimbus-ingress | Select-String "Address:|Host|/api|nimbus-backend|nimbus-frontend"

6) Live HTTP proof (frontend routing + backend health)
curl.exe -I http://nimbus.local/ | findstr /i "HTTP/"
curl.exe -i http://nimbus.local/api/health

7) Auth login + token + protected endpoint proof
$TOKEN = ( '{ "email": "test@user.com", "password": "test123" }' | curl.exe -s -H "Content-Type: application/json" --data-binary "@-" "http://nimbus.local/api/auth/login" | ConvertFrom-Json ).access_token
$TOKEN.Length
curl.exe -i -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" "http://nimbus.local/api/internal/secret-proof"

